Allocation instructions
=======================

None needed. Nothing has to be reserved, requested, or scheduled, and no
account of ours has to be shared with you.

Google Colab (recommended)
--------------------------
Open the notebook linked in infrastructure/url and choose Run all. Use a
standard CPU runtime; do not select a GPU, because nothing in the evaluation
uses one. The free tier is enough: the reproduction peaks at about 421 MB of
memory and finishes in about seven seconds, and the clone plus dependency
install dominate the wall clock.

Container (Chameleon, CloudLab, or a local Docker daemon)
---------------------------------------------------------
    docker build -t brave-new-browsing .
    docker run --rm --network none brave-new-browsing

A single small instance is enough. The build needs network access to install
four Python packages; the run itself is offline, which is why the command above
passes --network none.

Any Linux machine
-----------------
    bash install.sh
    PYTHON=$PWD/.venv/bin/python bash artifact/REPRODUCE.sh

One core, 1 GB of RAM, and about 500 MB of disk including the virtual
environment.

Credentials
-----------
None. The evaluation path makes no authenticated call, needs no API key, and
contacts no service of ours. The only network access in the whole process is
cloning this repository and installing four Python packages from PyPI.

Time budget
-----------
Well under the one day ACSAC allows for an evaluation task. See
infrastructure/resources for measured numbers.
